# Configuration for the Dropbear SSH server.
#
# This file is sourced by Buildroot's /etc/init.d/S50dropbear at boot; the
# contents of DROPBEAR_ARGS are appended to the dropbear command line.
#
# Root login policy for the Raspberry Kitchen Radio appliance:
#   * Root SSH login is ALLOWED. Dropbear permits root logins unless started
#     with "-w"; we deliberately do NOT pass "-w".
#   * Password authentication is ALLOWED. Dropbear enables it unless started
#     with "-s" (disable all passwords) or "-g" (disable password login for
#     root); we deliberately do NOT pass either.
#   * The root password itself is baked into the image via
#     BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ROOT_PASSWD ("radio") in the defconfig.
#
# NOTE: this is intentionally permissive because the device is a headless
# appliance on a trusted LAN. Change the root password (and consider switching
# to key-only auth by adding "-s") before exposing it to an untrusted network.
#
# -p 22   : listen on the standard SSH port.
DROPBEAR_ARGS="-p 22"
